<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ local body sale rule not yet in law - Peters.</title>
<headline>NZ local body sale rule not yet in law - Peters.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Treasurer Winston Peters said on Tuesday the coalition government's requirement for local bodies to win ratepayer and consumer approval before selling more than 24.9 percent of utilities did not yet apply.</p>
<p>&quot;Whilst we expect full implementation of this policy in the future, in the meantime the policy in existence prior to the coalition agreement prevails,&quot; Peters said in answer to questions in the House on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He said the coalition deal reflected the view that strategic assets should be retained and local government assets should only be sold with local approval.</p>
</text>
